; typeeditor.eval - the type editor builds a control for EVERY schema row, and a
; quest stage renamed a key at a time keeps every other stage's line
; (code-review C101, C100). Judged by tools/EditorTest.py phase 19.
;
; EditorTest writes, before this runs (into its scratch world, never the real
; one):
;   [et_stages]  stages = stage1 stage2
;                text_stage1 = The first line   text_stage2 = The second line
;
; 1. Every category with a schema opens on its first entry, the palette's
;    right-click path, and each row says what it built - read off the widget
;    tree: `typeset row <catalog> <key> <kind> <widgets>`. A kind the dialog's
;    switch did not know built nothing (monsters' dmgtype, effects'
;    damage_type).
; 2. stage2 becomes stage10 one keystroke at a time: "stage", then "stage1" -
;    another stage's id, which must be refused in the notice with nothing
;    moved - then "stage10". The working copy, the Save, and the entry read
;    back after it must all keep stage1's line.
; 3. The "taken" notice says what the fields SHOW, never what they once did.
;    Each section raises it ("stage1" typed over another stage), then:
;    - notice own:     the id typed back to its own stage's id - it comes down;
;    - notice rebuild: "+ Add a stage", whose rebuild resets every id field -
;                      it comes down;
;    - notice other:   the footer Delete's first click puts up ITS notice, then
;                      a unique id typed on a stage row - Delete's stays up;
;    - notice rows:    a third row still shows "stage1" while the second row
;                      takes a unique id - it stays up; the third row's own
;                      unique id then takes it down.
;    Nothing here is saved: the dialog is closed with `off`, which discards.

logecho on
reset
echo --- rows ---
typeset dialog rows all
echo --- stages ---
typeset dialog quests et_stages
typeset dialog stage 2 stage
typeset dialog stage 2 stage1
typeset dialog stage 2 stage10
typeset dialog fields
typeset dialog save
echo --- saved ---
typeset dialog quests et_stages
typeset dialog fields
echo --- notice own ---
typeset dialog stage 2 stage1
typeset dialog stage 2 stage10
echo --- notice rebuild ---
typeset dialog stage 2 stage1
typeset dialog stage add
echo --- notice other ---
typeset dialog stage 2 stage1
typeset dialog delete
typeset dialog stage 2 stage20
typeset dialog off
echo --- notice rows ---
typeset dialog quests et_stages
typeset dialog stage add
typeset dialog stage 3 stage1
typeset dialog stage 2 stage20
typeset dialog stage 3 stage30
typeset dialog off
